From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:44:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: round texture coordinates to zero when minifying with
 nearest

With round-to-nearest-even on, a nearest lookup takes the next texel for
the upper 2^-9 of each texel. panvk only turned it off when both filters
are nearest, so a nearest minify with a linear magnify filter still
rounded up; on the 1x1 level of a seamless cube that next texel is on
the neighbouring face. The Arm driver turns the rounding off whenever
the minification filter is nearest; do the same, as panfrost does.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_sampler.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_sampler.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_sampler.c
index ab6aa444c7b..5ca90fa6b5f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_sampler.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_sampler.c
@@ -127,12 +127,14 @@ panvk_sampler_fill_desc(const struct VkSamplerCreateInfo *info,
        * is used with VK_FILTER_NEAREST.
        *
        * Regardless, disabling round_to_nearest_even for NEAREST filters
-       * is a desirable precision improvement.
+       * is a desirable precision improvement. The Arm driver keys it on the
+       * minification filter alone: with a linear magnify filter, a nearest
+       * minify at the 1x1 level of a seamless cube would otherwise pick the
+       * neighbouring face near an edge.
        *
        * [1]: https://gitlab.khronos.org/Tracker/vk-gl-cts/-/issues/5547
        */
-      if (min_filter == VK_FILTER_NEAREST &&
-          mag_filter == VK_FILTER_NEAREST)
+      if (min_filter == VK_FILTER_NEAREST)
          cfg.round_to_nearest_even = false;
 
       cfg.lod_bias = info->mipLodBias;
